# HR-004: Expense Policy

**Document ID:** HR-004
**Version:** 1.0
**Effective Date:** January 1, 2026
**Owner:** HR & People Department
**Approver:** Finance & Legal Department

---

## 1. Policy Statement and Purpose

This Expense Policy establishes the guidelines and procedures for the reimbursement of business-related expenses incurred by employees of MedSync Health. The purpose is to ensure that all expenses are necessary, reasonable, and incurred in the best interest of the company, while maintaining compliance with all relevant tax and regulatory requirements.

Given MedSync Health's current financial position, with a **Net Margin of -4.6%** (FY 2024), adherence to this policy is critical for fiscal responsibility and achieving our goal of a successful IPO.

## 2. Scope and Eligibility

This policy applies to all full-time and part-time employees of MedSync Health, regardless of their location (Boston, London, Berlin, Singapore) or employment level. All expenses must be submitted through the designated expense management system.

## 3. General Principles

### 3.1. Currency and Reimbursement

All expense claims must be submitted in the currency in which they were incurred. Reimbursement will be processed in the employee's local payroll currency, using the exchange rate on the date the expense was incurred. All limits specified in this document are in **United Arab Emirates Dirham (AED)**, which serves as the company's internal financial benchmark.

### 3.2. Approval Process

All expense reports require approval from the employee's direct manager. Expenses exceeding the standard limits or requiring exception must be approved by the next level of management (Director or VP) and ultimately by the **Finance & Legal Department**.

| Employee Level | Standard Approval | Exception Approval |
|:---------------|:------------------|:-------------------|
| IC | Manager | Director/VP |
| Manager | Director | VP |
| Director | VP | CFO (Michael Rodriguez) |
| VP | CFO (Michael Rodriguez) | CEO (Dr. Sarah Chen) |

### 3.3. Required Documentation

All expense claims must be accompanied by original receipts or invoices. Expenses under **AED 36.75** (equivalent to $10 USD) may be claimed without a receipt, provided a detailed explanation is included.

## 4. Expense Categories and Limits (AED)

Expense limits are tiered based on the employee's organizational level to reflect varying business needs and responsibilities.

### 4.1. Business Travel and Accommodation

| Category | IC / Manager | Director | VP / C-Level | Policy Detail |
|:---|:---|:---|:---|:---|
| **Airfare** | Economy Class | Premium Economy/Business Class (for flights > 6 hours) | Business Class | Must book at least 14 days in advance. |
| **Hotel (Per Night)** | Up to **AED 735** | Up to **AED 1,102.50** | Up to **AED 1,470** | Must use preferred corporate rates. |
| **Per Diem (Meals)** | **AED 183.75** | **AED 257.25** | **AED 367.50** | Covers all meals and incidentals. Receipts not required for Per Diem. |
| **Ground Transportation** | Economy (Taxi/Ride-share) | Business (Taxi/Ride-share) | Business/First Class Train | Must be cost-effective. Personal car mileage is reimbursed at **AED 1.84/km**. |

### 4.2. Business Meals and Entertainment

Expenses for entertaining clients, partners, or team members must have a clear business purpose and include a list of attendees.

| Category | IC / Manager | Director | VP / C-Level | Policy Detail |
|:---|:---|:---|:---|:---|
| **Client Meal (Per Person)** | Up to **AED 294** | Up to **AED 441** | Up to **AED 735** | Must be pre-approved by Manager. |
| **Internal Team Meal** | Up to **AED 110.25** | Up to **AED 147** | Up to **AED 183.75** | Must be for a specific business purpose (e.g., working lunch). |

### 4.3. Professional Development and Training

MedSync Health supports professional growth. All training, conference fees, and certification costs must be pre-approved.

| Category | IC / Manager | Director | VP / C-Level | Policy Detail |
|:---|:---|:---|:---|:---|
| **Annual Training Budget** | **AED 7,350** | **AED 11,025** | **AED 14,700** | Unused budget does not roll over. |

## 5. Non-Reimbursable Expenses

The following expenses are generally **not** reimbursable:

*   Personal travel, including spouse/family travel.
*   Fines, penalties, or parking tickets.
*   Personal items (e.g., clothing, toiletries, gifts for personal use).
*   Alcoholic beverages, except when entertaining clients within the approved limit.

